hadiths[43]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1068","Masruq says: We asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) about this verse: ""Do not think of those who are killed in the way of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, being provided for."" So Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We asked about this verse (from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him), and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The souls of the martyrs are in the bodies of green birds, inside lanterns hanging from the Throne, and they roam freely in Paradise wherever they wish, then return to their lanterns. Once, their Lord looked at them and said: Do you desire anything? They said: What more could we desire? We roam freely in Paradise wherever we wish. But their Lord, Glorified and Exalted, asked them three times. When they saw that they would not be left without making a request (i.e., their Lord kept asking), they said: O our Lord! We wish that our souls be returned to our bodies (i.e., our worldly bodies) so that we may be killed again in Your path. When their Lord saw that they had no other wish, He left them as they were."
"1069","´Sayyiduna Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qais narrates from his father that` I heard my father saying in front of the enemy (i.e., in the battlefield) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is under the shade of swords. Upon hearing this, a poor man with worn-out clothes stood up and said, ""O Abu Musa, did you (yourself) hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say this?"" (Sayyiduna Abu Musa) said: Yes. The narrator says, upon hearing this, he went to his companions and said, ""I bid you farewell,"" and broke the sheath of his sword, then took the sword and advanced towards the enemy, striking them with his sword until he was martyred."
"1070","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah guarantees the one who goes out in His path, and does not go out except for jihad and believes in Allah and affirms His messengers. (Allah has said that) such a person is under My protection: either I will admit him to Paradise, or I will return him to his home with reward and spoils of war. By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), there is no wound inflicted in the path of Allah except that it will come on the Day of Resurrection in the same state as it was in the world—its color will be the color of blood, but its fragrance will be that of musk. By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), if it were not hard upon the Muslims, I would never stay behind any expedition that fights in the path of Allah. But I do not have enough means (of conveyance, etc.), nor do the Muslims have enough means (of conveyance, etc.), and if I were to go, it would be hard for some Muslims to remain behind. By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I wish that I could fight in the path of Allah, then be killed, then fight again, then be killed, then fight again, then be killed."
"1071","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Sa'id! Whoever is pleased with Allah as his Lord, with Islam as his religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as his Prophet, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) was astonished and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Please say it again."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated it and then said: There is another deed by which a servant will receive one hundred ranks in Paradise, and the distance between each rank is as great as the distance between the sky and the earth. Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""What is that deed?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Striving in the path of Allah, striving in the path of Allah."
"1072","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked, ""Which person is the best?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""The one who strives in the way of Allah with his wealth and his life."" He asked, ""Then who?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied, ""A believer who worships Allah in a mountain pass and keeps people safe from his harm."
"1073","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies without having fought in jihad or having intended to fight in jihad, dies on a branch of hypocrisy. Abdullah bin Saheem (the narrator of the hadith) says that Abdullah bin Mubarak said: We think that this hadith pertains to the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (This is the opinion of Ibn Mubarak. Allama Albani has written that there is no evidence to restrict it to the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him.)"
"1074","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Umm Haram bint Milhan, who was married to Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him). (Because she was a mahram to the Prophet, i.e., his foster maternal aunt or the aunt of his father or grandfather.) She used to feed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One day, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to her, and she fed him and began to look for lice in his head. During this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell asleep. Then he woke up smiling, so Umm Haram asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Why are you smiling?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Some people from my Ummah were shown to me, who were riding in the middle of the sea in the way of Allah, as kings ride on thrones or like kings on thrones."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah that He makes me among them."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, then he rested his head and slept again, and then woke up smiling. I asked, ""Why are you smiling, O Messenger of Allah?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Some people from my Ummah were shown to me, who were going out for jihad,"" and he described as above. I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah that He makes me among those people."" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""You will be among the first group."" Then Umm Haram bint Milhan (may Allah be pleased with her) set out by sea (to conquer the island of Cyprus) during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) (which, after thirteen hundred years, the Sultan of Rome handed over to the English), and when she was about to disembark from the river, she fell from her mount and was martyred."
"1075","Sayedna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Guarding for one day and night in the way of Allah is better than fasting and worshipping for a whole month, and if he dies during this, his deed will continue (i.e., its reward will not cease after death but will keep increasing; this is specific to this deed), and his provision will continue (which is given to martyrs), and he will be safe from the people of tribulation (i.e., from the trial of the angels in the grave, or the punishment of the grave, or the whisperings of Satan at the time of death)."
"1076","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: To go out in the morning or evening in the path of Allah is better than the world and whatever is in it."
"1077","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was sitting by the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man said: I do not care about any deed after becoming a Muslim, as long as I give water to the pilgrims. Another said: What do I care about any deed after Islam, as long as I maintain the Sacred Mosque. A third said: Jihad is better than these things. Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) rebuked them and said: Do not raise your voices before the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Jumu’ah, but after the Jumu’ah prayer I will ask the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about the matter in which you have differed. Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: “Do you consider the providing of water to the pilgrims and the maintenance of al-Masjid al-Haram as equal to the deeds of one who believes in Allah and the Last Day and strives in the way of Allah? ...” (al-Tawbah: 19) to the end of the verse."
"1078","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Hunaif (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sincerely asks Allah for martyrdom, Allah will grant him the rank of the martyrs even if he dies on his bed."
"1079","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: Whoever enters Paradise will not wish to return to the world, even if he were given all that is on the earth, but the martyr will wish to return and be killed ten times because of the honor and reward he sees (due to martyrdom). (That is, he will wish to attain it again and again.)"
"1080","`Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Actions are judged by intentions, and every person will have only what he intended. So whoever's migration was for Allah and His Messenger, then his migration is for Allah and His Messenger. And whoever migrated for worldly gain or to marry a woman, then his migration is for that for which he migrated."
"1081","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""Send some men with us who will teach us the Qur'an and Sunnah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent seventy men from among the Ansar to them. They were called the Qurra (reciters and memorizers of the Qur'an), and among them was my maternal uncle Haram (may Allah be pleased with him). These Qurra used to recite the Qur'an and would gather at night to teach and learn from each other. During the day, they would bring water and place it in the mosque, and they would collect wood (from the forest), sell it, and buy food with its price to feed the people of Suffah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent them to the people (who had requested some men for teaching). But before they reached the area to which they had been invited, those people martyred the Qurra. The Qurra said, ""Allahumma balligh 'anna nabiyyana..."" etc., meaning, ""O Allah, convey from us to our Prophet that we have met Allah, and we are pleased with Allah and Allah is pleased with us."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a disbeliever came to my uncle Haram (may Allah be pleased with him) and struck him from behind with a spear, piercing him through. Sayyiduna Haram (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Fuztu wa rabbil Ka'bah,"" meaning, ""By the Lord of the Ka'bah, I have succeeded."" Then (when this incident had occurred), the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Your (Muslim) brothers have been martyred, and they have sent this message: We have met Allah, we are pleased with Allah, and He is pleased with us."
"1082","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man was walking when he saw a thorny branch on the road, so he removed it (from the road). Because of this, Allah rewarded him by forgiving him. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that there are five types of martyrs: the one who dies of plague (an epidemic, in that time plague was caused by vomiting and diarrhea), the one who dies of a stomach illness (such as diarrhea, dysentery, or dropsy), the one who drowns, the one who is crushed to death, and the one who is killed in the way of Allah."
"1083","Lady Hafsa bint Sirin says: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) asked me, ""What illness did Yahya bin Abi Amrah die of?"" I replied, ""He died of plague."" He said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Plague is martyrdom for every Muslim."
"1084","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every sin of a martyr is forgiven except debt."
"1085","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he stood among the companions (to deliver a sermon) and informed them that the most virtuous of all deeds is striving in the way of Allah and having faith in Allah the Exalted. A man stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If I am killed in the way of Allah, will my sins be erased from me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Yes, if you are killed in the way of Allah, with patience, and your intention is purely for Allah the Exalted, and you remain facing (the enemy) and do not turn your back."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""What did you say?"" He replied, ""If I am killed in the way of Allah, will my sins be forgiven?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) again said, ""Yes, if you are killed with patience, with a pure intention, and your face is towards (the enemy) and you do not turn your back, except for debt, for Jibreel (peace be upon him) has informed me of this."
"1086","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you say if someone comes to take my wealth (unjustly)?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Do not give him your wealth."" He then asked, ""What if he fights me?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Then fight him."" He asked, ""What if he kills me?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Then you are a martyr."" He asked, ""What if I kill him?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Then he will go to Hell."
"1087","Thabit says that Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that my uncle, after whom I was named (that is, his name was also Anas), could not participate in the Battle of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). And this matter was very hard on him, and he said: ""I was absent from the first battle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Now, if Allah grants me another battle with you (O Messenger of Allah), then Allah will see what I do."" And he refrained from saying anything else (meaning, he was afraid to make any further claims, such as saying, ""I will do this or that,"" because perhaps he might not be able to fulfill it and would be counted among the liars). Then he went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to the Battle of Uhud. The narrator says that Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) came before him (and in the narration of Bukhari, it is mentioned that he was retreating after defeat), so Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him, ""O Abu Amr"" (this was the kunyah of Sa'd bin Mu'adh, may Allah be pleased with him), ""where are you going?"" Then (without waiting for his reply, he himself said), ""I am smelling the fragrance of Paradise from behind Uhud."" Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said that then he fought the disbelievers until he was martyred. (After the battle) it was seen that there were more than eighty (80) wounds of swords, spears, and arrows on his body. His sister, that is, my paternal aunt, Rubayyi' bint Nadr, said: ""I did not recognize my brother except by looking at the tips of his fingers (because his whole body was torn apart by wounds)."" And this verse was revealed: ""Among the believers are men who have been true to their covenant with Allah... some of them have fulfilled their vow, and some are still waiting, but they have not changed in the least."" The companions used to say that this verse was revealed about him and his companions."
"1088","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! A man fights for loot, a man fights for fame, and a man fights to show his status—so which one is fighting in the way of Allah?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is exalted, he is the one who fights in the way of Allah."
"1089","Sulaiman bin Yasar says that when the people departed from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), Natil, who was from the people of Syria (Natil bin Qais Kharami, he was from Palestine and a Tabi'i, his father was a companion), said, ""O Sheikh! Narrate to me a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Alright, I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he used to say: The first person whose case will be decided on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who was martyred. When he will be brought before Allah, Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. Allah will ask, 'What did you do for them?' He will say, 'I fought in Your way until I was martyred.' Allah will say, 'You have lied. You fought so that people would call you brave, and you were called brave.' Then it will be ordered, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into Hell. And there will be a man who acquired knowledge, taught it, and recited the Qur'an. He will be brought before Allah. Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. Then it will be said, 'What did you do for them?' He will say, 'I acquired knowledge, taught it, and recited the Qur'an.' Allah will say, 'You have lied. You acquired knowledge so that people would call you a scholar, and you recited the Qur'an so that people would call you a reciter. In the world, you were called a scholar and a reciter.' Then it will be ordered, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into Hell. And there will be a man to whom Allah had given all kinds of wealth. He will be brought before Allah. Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. Then Allah will ask, 'What did you do for them?' He will say, 'I did not leave any way in which You like wealth to be spent except that I spent in it for Your sake.' Allah will say, 'You are lying. You spent so that people would call you generous, and people called you generous in the world.' Then it will be ordered, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into Hell."
"1090","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man from Banu Nabit (a tribe of the Ansar) came and said: I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah, and that you (O Prophet ﷺ) are His servant and His messenger. Then he advanced and kept fighting until he was killed. The Prophet ﷺ said: He did little deeds but attained great reward."
"1091","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If an army or a detachment fights in jihad, then obtains spoils and returns safely, then two-thirds of its reward in the Hereafter has been given to it in this world. And if an army or a detachment returns empty-handed and suffers loss (i.e., is wounded or killed), then it will receive its full reward in the Hereafter."
"1092","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Khalid al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah has (himself) performed jihad, and whoever looks after the family of a warrior, he too has performed jihad (i.e., he has earned the reward of jihad)."
"1093","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that a young man from the tribe of Aslam said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I intend to go for jihad but I do not have the necessary equipment."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Go to so-and-so; he had prepared equipment for jihad but he has fallen ill."" He went to that person and said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conveys his greetings to you and says: Give me that equipment."" He (the sick man) said (to his wife or slave woman), ""O so-and-so! Give him all the equipment and do not keep anything back. By Allah, do not keep anything back, for there will be blessing in it for you."
"1094","‘Sayyiduna Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrates from his father (may Allah be pleased with him)’: He said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The sanctity of the women of the Mujahideen for those who stay at home is like the sanctity of their own mothers. And whoever stays at home and looks after the family and property of a Mujahid, then betrays in it, he will be made to stand on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to the Mujahid: Take from his deeds whatever you wish. (Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) What do you think?"
"1095","`Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A group from my Ummah will always remain steadfast on the truth; no one will be able to harm them, until the command of Allah comes (i.e., the Day of Judgment) and they will be in that state (i.e., dominant and upon the truth)."
"1096","Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Shumasah Mahri says: I was sitting with Muslamah bin Makhlad and with him was Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him). Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Hour will not be established except upon the worst of creatures, and they will be worse than those of the Age of Ignorance. Whatever they pray to Allah for, Allah will grant them. They were in this state when Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so Muslamah said to him: O Uqbah! Did you hear what Abdullah is saying? Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He knows better than me, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: A group or a party from my Ummah will always fight upon the command of Allah, and will prevail over their enemy. Whoever opposes them will not be able to harm them, until the Hour comes and they are in that state. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said so). Then Allah will send a wind which will have the fragrance of musk and will touch the body like silk. It will not leave anyone whose heart has even a grain's weight of faith, except that it will cause him to die. After that, only the worst (disbelieving) people will remain, and upon them the Hour will be established."
"1097","The conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The people of the West (i.e., the Arabs or the people of Syria) will always remain dominant upon the truth, until the Day of Resurrection is established."
"1098","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, laughs at two persons; one killed the other, yet both enter Paradise. The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! How will this happen? He (peace be upon him) said: One fought in the way of Allah and was martyred. Then the one who killed him embraced Islam, fought in the way of Allah, and was martyred."
"1099","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Both will not be gathered together in Hell in such a way that they would harm each other. The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who are those people?"" He (peace be upon him) said: The Muslim who kills a disbeliever, then remains steadfast upon righteousness."
"1100","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a man brought a she-camel with its bridle and said, ""I give this in the way of Allah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""In exchange for this, you will receive seven hundred she-camels with bridles on the Day of Resurrection."
"1101","Sidna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My (riding) animal is gone, now please provide me with a mount."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I do not have a mount."" A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall I tell him of someone who will give him a mount?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Whoever guides to a good deed, for him is a reward equal to that of the one who does it."
"1102","‘Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the pulpit explaining the statement of Allah, “Prepare against them whatever force you can.” He was saying: “Be aware! Force means archery. Be aware! Force means archery. (Then again) Be aware! Force means archery.”"
"1103","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""Soon, several lands will be conquered at your hands, and Allah Almighty will suffice for you. Then, none of you should abandon the practice of archery (that is, learning marksmanship: with pistols, Kalashnikovs, rockets, missiles, etc.)."
"1104","‘It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Shumasah that Faqim Lakhmi said to Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him): “In this old age, you go to and from these two targets; it must be difficult for you.” Sayyiduna Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “If I had not heard one thing from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I would not have borne this hardship.” Harith said: “I asked Ibn Shumasah, ‘What was that thing?’ He said: ‘The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever learns archery and then abandons it, he is not from us, or he is sinful.’”"
"1105","Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) rubbing the forelock of a horse with his finger and saying: Blessing is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, that is, reward and spoils (goodness of both this world and the Hereafter)."
"1106","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is blessing in the forelocks of horses."
"1107","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the ""ashkal"" horse. In another narration, it is mentioned that an ""ashkal"" horse is one whose right leg and left foreleg are white, or whose right foreleg and left leg are white. (And according to the linguists, the correct definition is that ""ashkal"" refers to a horse whose three legs are white, but there is no whiteness above.)"
"1108","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) held a race between the trained horses from Hafya to Thaniyyatul Wada‘ (the distance between these two places is five or six miles, and some have said six or seven miles), and set the race for untrained horses from Thaniyya to the mosque of Banu Zuraiq. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was among those who competed in horse riding."
"1109","Abu Ishaq says that he heard from Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding this verse: “Those Muslims who sit (at home) and those who fight (in Allah’s cause) are not equal (i.e., the rank of those who fight is much greater),” that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed Sayyiduna Zaid to bring a bone, and he wrote this verse on it. Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umm Maktum complained about his blindness (i.e., I am blind, so I cannot go for jihad; will my rank be less because of this?). At that time, these words were revealed: “those who are not disabled” (and the disabled will be equal in rank to the mujahideen)."
"1110","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a battle when he said: ""There are some people in Madinah who, whenever you walk or cross any valley, they are with you (that is, they receive the same reward as you do). (These are the people) who could not come with you due to illness."
